# class Vec { x; get length() { return this.x } }   class Leaky { get length() { kept = this; return 1 } }   class Self { get length() { return this } }
# function measure(v) { return v.length }   measure(new Vec);  measure(new Leaky);  measure(new Self)
# Of `measure` the link says that it reads `length` out of its parameter and returns what it finds. Only the caller knows the object. Where the read can find nothing but a getter that a class defines for good,
# the getter is entered with the operand as `this`: what it reads there is read, and where it keeps `this` the operand is kept. What it returns is what `measure` has read through the operand,
# so the object that `Self` answers is returned like that.
# RUN: fates-at-calls
# CHECK: f0 v19 Call operand 2: members-read contents=returned read=["x", "length"]
# CHECK: f0 v20 Call operand 2: stored-in-variable+members-read contents=returned read=["length"]
# CHECK: f0 v21 Call operand 2: returned+members-read contents=returned results=[any] read=["length"]

